# Global entries below apply to every authenticated client (mosquitto
# evaluates them in addition to any matching "user" block).
#
# Every FBF site publishes telemetry to fbf/#, and per multi-site.mdx's
# "Reaching back into a site" design, a site's command channel is scoped
# to its own username via %u - a site can only read/write cmd/<its own
# username>/#, never another site's. This is the actual security boundary
# the command channel needs; telemetry write access is intentionally
# shared, matching today's behavior before auth existed.
topic write fbf/#
pattern readwrite cmd/%u/#

# The trusted central stack (mqtt_listener, fault_detector,
# derivation_engine, and integration tests standing in for them) - same
# Docker network as today's anonymous access, just now authenticated.
user timberdoodle
topic readwrite #
